sentences.text:
Basically only three facts need to be established by the claimants for assessing compensation in the case of death :
(a) age of the deceased;
(b) income of the deceased; and the (c) the number of dependents.

Having regard to the facts and circumstances of the case, it is hereby ordered that out of total compensation amount, the amount is disbursed as follows :
(a) Petitioner No.1/Smt. Meenu Devi (Wife of deceased Ashok Kumar) shall be entitled to share amount of Rs.6,00,000/ (Rupees Six Lakhs Only) alongwith proportionate interest;
(b) Petitioner No.2/Ms. Santi Devi (Mother of deceased Ashok Kumar) shall be entitled to share amount of Rs.3,22,330/ (Rupees Three Lakhs Tewenty Two Thousand Three Hundred Thirty Only) alongwith proportionate interest;
(c) Petitioner No.3/Master Harsh (Minor son of deceased Ashok Kumar) shall be entitled to share amount of Rs.5,00,000/ (Rupees Five Lakhs Only) alongwith proportionate interest;
(d) Petitioner No.4/Disha (Minor daughter of deceased Ashok Kumar) shall be entitled to share amount of Rs.5,00,000/ (Rupees Five Lakhs Only) alongwith proportionate interest;
MACT No. 3982022 Meenu Devi & ors. v. Sanjay Mandal & Ors.
37.

